{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm-consumers.implementation-plan.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t\n     2\t# yin.vm consumers — the deletion plan\n     3\t\n     4\tStatus: implementation plan for deleting the experimental v1 VM models\n     5\t(`yin.vm.{semantic, register, stack, space}`) and the macro engine\n     6\t(`yin.vm.macro`), with every file that requires them either deleted or\n     7\tmigrated so the build stays green. Subordinate to\n     8\t[`yin.vm.divergence-register.md`](./yin.vm.divergence-register.md),\n     9\t[`dao.runtime.implementation-plan.md`](./dao.runtime.implementation-plan.md)\n    10\tand [`dao.stream.md`](./dao.stream.md).\n    11\t\n    12\tRevised 2026-09-10, two architect rounds: r1 against a consumer sweep of the\n    13\ttree, r2 against an independent adversarial review of r1. The first draft\n    14\tnamed two files to check for stale references; the census now holds\n    15\tthirty-one. The revision history at the end records what each round changed.\n    16\t\n    17\t## The problem and context\n    18\t\n    19\tThe divergence register scopes `yin.vm` to the ast-walker slice:\n    20\t\"`semantic`, `register`, `stack`, `space`, `macro` and `wasm` are not ported,\n    21\tso nothing here speaks for them\" (`yin.vm.divergence-register.md:20-21`).\n    22\tThe v2 corpus is macro-free by construction (its change 2), and `yin.repl`\n    23\tships one evaluator (its change 1). Porting the experimental models to\n    24\t`dao.stream` would be a rewrite of each for no consumer; they are deleted.\n    25\t\n    26\t`dao.stream.md:806-808` records the decision: \"The v1 VM lineage is deleted\n    27\trather than migrated, under `yin.vm-consumers.implementation-plan.md`,\n    28\tbecause a v2 twin already exists for every one of its consumers.\" This plan\n    29\tis the first slice of that deletion — the models that have no v2 twin and no\n    30\tplace in the ast-walker scope. It is not the whole v1 lineage; see *Boundary*.\n    31\t\n    32\t## What is verified and what is judged\n    33\t\n    34\tEverything in the census below is a verified fact from a `grep`/`git` sweep\n    35\ton 2026-09-10 unless marked **[J]** (judgment call). Facts the r2 reviewer\n    36\tfound and this round re-verified are marked **[R]**. Line numbers are as of\n    37\tthe sweep.\n    38\t\n    39\t### The wasm entry is already gone\n    40\t\n    41\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/wasm.cljc` and `test/yin/vm/wasm_test.cljc` were deleted in\n    42\tcommit `b8a6fce` (\"docs(vm): remove wasm backend as it is out of scope\",\n    43\t2026-09-08, 854 lines). Neither was moved or renamed; no `wasm.clj*` exists\n    44\tunder `src/` or `test/`. The first draft of this plan listed both for\n    45\tdeletion; they are dropped from the delete list. Residue that still names the\n    46\tbackend: `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/wasm-vm.md` (a whole document for a deleted\n    47\tbackend) and `docs/agy-test.md:59,104`. Build outputs under `.shadow-cljs/`\n    48\tand `lib/cljd-out/` still carry `wasm` artifacts, but `lib/cljd-out` has zero\n    49\tgit-tracked files, so there is nothing to delete from the repository.\n    50\t\n    51\t### Dependency order between the VMs and the macro engine\n    52\t\n    53\t`yin.vm.macro` requires only `dao.datom` and `yin.vm` (`macro.cljc:12-13`).\n    54\tThe four VMs require it: `semantic.cljc:11`, `register.cljc:26`,\n    55\t`stack.cljc:27`, `space.cljc:70`. `register`, `stack` and `space` also require\n    56\t`semantic`. Nothing else under `src/` requires `macro`; `yang.clojure` emits\n    57\t`:yin/macro-expand` nodes but does not require the engine.\n    58\t\n    59\tSo `macro` is a leaf *below* the VMs: deleting the VMs first leaves `macro`\n    60\tcompiling but orphaned, and deleting `macro` first breaks all four VMs. The\n    61\tfirst draft's order (VMs, then macro) was dependency-correct for `src/` but\n    62\twrong for `test/`: `test/yin/vm/macro_test.cljc` requires `register`,\n    63\t`semantic`, `space` and `stack` (`:10-13`) and `test/yang/macro_test.clj`\n    64\trequires `semantic` (`:9`), so both macro tests break the moment the VMs go\n    65\tand cannot wait for a \"Phase 2\". The two phases are collapsed into one\n    66\tdeletion set, landed as one change.\n    67\t\n    68\t### What the sweep has to cover\n    69\t\n    70\tr1's census was built from a namespace grep over `.clj*` sources and missed\n    71\tthree things the r2 review caught: a test that requires the models directly\n    72\t(finding 1), an explicit `:vm-type :semantic` argument in a `.cljd` host file\n    73\t(finding 2), and a Dart launcher under `bin/` plus an alias count in\n    74\t`deps.edn` (finding 3). None of them is a namespace `:require` in a `.clj*`\n    75\tfile, which is all the r1 sweep looked for. The Phase 0 sweep is therefore\n    76\tthree greps, not one, and its scope is `src test bin deps.edn bb.edn\n    77\tshadow-cljs.edn public`, not `src test`.\n    78\t\n    79\t## Consumer census\n    80\t\n    81\tEvery file that requires a deleted namespace, names a deleted model, or\n    82\tlaunches deleted code, grouped by disposition. The brief's sweep listed three\n    83\tlive consumers; there are nine non-test, non-benchmark ones.\n    84\t\n    85\t### Deleted with their dependency\n    86\t\n    87\t| file | requires | why deletion, not migration |\n    88\t|---|---|---|\n    89\t| `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc` | `macro` | the model itself |\n    90\t| `src/cljc/yin/vm/register.cljc` | `macro`, `semantic` | the model itself |\n    91\t| `src/cljc/yin/vm/stack.cljc` | `macro`, `semantic` | the model itself |\n    92\t| `src/cljc/yin/vm/space.cljc` | `macro`, `semantic` | the model itself |\n    93\t| `src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc` | — | leaf; required only by the four above |\n    94\t| `src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff.cljc` | `register`, `stack` | **[J]** no `src/` consumer at all — only its own test requires it. Its v2 twin `continuation_handoff_v2.cljc` is what `continuation_stream_v2.cljs:36` uses. Migration already happened; this is the residue |\n    95\t| `src/clj/yin/demo.clj` | `register` | **[J]** twin `yin.demo-v2` (`demo_v2.clj:27-29`, on `yin.vm`) exists; no `deps.edn` alias or doc runs `yin.demo`; the only run instruction is its own docstring |\n    96\t| `src/cljs/datomworld/demo/compilation_pipeline.cljs` | `register`, `semantic`, `stack` | **[J]** twin `compilation_pipeline_v2.cljs` is wired into `datomworld.demo` beside it — but the twin lacks the Python and PHP frontends; see D3, which closes that gap before this file goes |\n    97\t| `src/cljs/datomworld/demo/continuation_stream.cljs` | `register`, `stack` | **[J]** twin `continuation_stream_v2.cljs`, wired in; feature diff owed in Phase 0 |\n    98\t| `src/cljs/datomworld/demo/equation_plotter.cljs` | `register` | **[J]** twin `equation_plotter_v2.cljs`, wired in; feature diff owed in Phase 0 |\n    99\t| `src/cljd/yin/register_bench_cljd.cljd` | `register` | benchmark of a deleted model; no `bb.edn`/`deps.edn` entry compiles it |\n   100\t| `bin/register_bench_cljd.dart` | imports `lib/cljd-out/yin/register-bench-cljd.dart`, the compiled output of the file above | **[R]** a Dart launcher for a deleted bench; goes with it. Its twin `bin/register_bench_cljd_v2.dart` (for `src/cljd/yin/register_bench_cljd_v2.cljd`) stays. `bin/yin_repl_main.dart` imports v1 `repl.dart` and stays under D1 |\n   101\t| `src/clj/yin/vm/bytecode_bench.clj` | `space`, `register`, `semantic`, `stack`, `ast-walker` | **[J]** it exists to compare the bytecode models against the walker (`--register-only`, `--stack-only`, `--semantic-only`, `--cesk-space-only`); with one model left it compares nothing. Delete rather than trim to `--ast-walker-only`. **[R]** Its **five** `deps.edn` aliases go with it: `:bench`, `:profile`, `:profile-fast`, `:profile-cesk-space`, `:profile-ast-walker` (`deps.edn:17-30`; r1 said four). A v2 walker bench, if wanted, is a new file under the VM plan |\n   102\t\n   103\t### Migrated to keep working without the deleted VMs\n   104\t\n   105\t| file | change |\n   106\t|---|---|\n   107\t| `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc` | drop the three requires (`:19-21`); `vm-constructors` (`:33-37`) and `vm-labels` (`:40-44`) shrink to `:ast-walker`; `create-state`'s default `vm-type :semantic` (`:183`) becomes `:ast-walker`; both `help-text` branches (`:65`, `:74`) read `(vm :ast-walker)`. Nothing else in the file names a model. See D1 for why migrate and not delete |\n   108\t| `src/cljd/yin/repl/flutter.cljd` | **[R]** `start-server!` calls `(repl/create-state {:vm-type :semantic})` at `:60` — an explicit argument, untouched by the default change, and `make-vm` throws \"Unknown Yin REPL VM type\" the moment `:semantic` is gone. Both Flutter demos take this path at startup (`dao_gui.cljd:321`, `solar_system.cljd:123`). **[J]** Change the call to `(repl/create-state {})` so the widget takes the REPL's default and never names a model again. See D1 for how this class of defect is caught |\n   109\t| `src/cljs/datomworld/demo.cljs` | drop the three v1 demo requires (`:2`, `:4`, `:8`), their picker cards (`:32-45`, `:62-…`, the `:pipeline`, `:continuation`, `:plotter` entries), and their `case` branches (`:230,232,234`). In `demo->hash` (`:95,97,99`) drop the three v1 rows. In `hash->demo` (`:77,79,81`) **keep** `\"#pipeline\"`, `\"#plotter\"`, `\"#continuation\"` and point them at `:pipeline-v2`, `:plotter-v2`, `:continuation-v2` — see D5. The `-v2` ids stay as they are; renaming them is not this plan's |\n   110\t| `src/cljs/datomworld/demo/compilation_pipeline_v2.cljs` | receives the Python and PHP frontends from v1 before v1 is deleted — see D3 |\n   111\t| `test/yin/vm/test_utils.cljc` | `vm-factories` (`:14-18`) becomes `{:ast-walker ast-walker/create-vm}`; drop the four requires (`:5-8`). `run-all-vms`, `queue-vm`, `queue-ast` are unchanged |\n   112\t| `test/yin/vm/runtime_regression_test.cljc` | **[R]** r1 listed this as unchanged; it requires `register`, `semantic`, `stack` directly (`:8-10`). Verified this round: the body never uses those aliases — every deftest iterates `vtu/vm-factories` (`:17`, `:46`, `:84`, `:121`). Drop the three requires; nothing else changes, and the tests keep running over the walker alone until `dao.runtime` R4 deletes the file |\n   113\t| `test/yin/vm/telemetry_test.cljc` | `eval-emits-step-and-halt-snapshots-across-cljc-vms-test` (`:50-56`) iterates a four-model map; reduce it to `:ast-walker` and drop the three requires (`:7-9`). The other four deftests already use only the walker |\n   114\t| `test/yin/repl_test.cljc` | `(vm :register)` at `:103` and `:142` becomes `(vm :ast-walker)` and the `\"RegisterVM\"` label assertion becomes `\"ASTWalkerVM\"`; the three `:semantic` default assertions at `:272`, `:296`, `:312` become `:ast-walker`. Add one deftest, see D1 |\n   115\t\n   116\t### Deleted test suites\n   117\t\n   118\t| file | why |\n   119\t|---|---|\n   120\t| `test/yin/vm/semantic_test.cljc`, `register_test.cljc`, `stack_test.cljc`, `space_test.cljc` | contracts of deleted models. The first draft named only `space_test` |\n   121\t| `test/yin/vm/macro_test.cljc` | contract of the deleted engine; requires all four models |\n   122\t| `test/yang/macro_test.clj` | 3 of 4 deftests go through `semantic` with a macro registry. **[J]** the one walker-only test, `test-nested-defn-ast-walker` (`:186-196`), exercises `yang.clojure/compile-program` on nested `defn` and does not need macros; move it and the `compile-program-and-run` helper (`:23-30`) into `test/yang/clojure_test.clj` rather than lose it |\n   123\t| `test/yin/vm/parity_test.cljc` (v1) | 15 of 16 deftests compare the walker against the four models; the 16th, `stream-make-default-capacity-parity-test`, compares the walker's capacity to theirs. With one model there is no parity to assert. Delete whole. v2 parity is `test/yin/vm/parity_test.cljc`, which requires v1 `ast-walker` only (`:16`) and is untouched |\n   124\t| `test/yin/vm/stream_listen_test.cljc` | its `datom-vms` factory (`:16-20`) is `semantic`/`register`/`stack` only; the walker is not in it. Delete whole. Ingress-on-a-stream for the walker is covered by `stream_driver_test` (v1) and `yin.vm.stream-observer`'s tests |\n   125\t| `test/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff_test.cljc` | tests a deleted file |\n   126\t| `test/datomworld/demo/vm_state_keys_test.cljs` | requires `continuation-stream` (v1), `register`, `stack` |\n   127\t\n   128\t### Unchanged, named so the reader can check\n   129\t\n   130\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/{ast_walker, engine, ffi, telemetry, stream_driver,\n   131\truntime_adapter}.cljc` and `src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc` do not require any deleted\n   132\tnamespace and stay (see *Boundary*). `public/chp/yin.chp:18` links to\n   133\t`/demo.html#pipeline` and is left as written because D5 keeps that hash\n   134\tworking.\n   135\t\n   136\t## Decisions\n   137\t\n   138\t### D1 — v1 `yin.repl` is migrated to `:ast-walker`, not deleted here [J]\n   139\t\n   140\tThe brief asked whether v1 `yin.repl` is \"fully superseded by `yin.repl`\n   141\tand slated for its own deletion under a different plan\". Verified against the\n   142\ttree:\n   143\t\n   144\t- `yin.repl` is a twin, not an in-place migration\n   145\t  (`dao.jing.remote.implementation-plan.md:90-92`;\n   146\t  `yin.repl.implementation-plan.md:17-22` says v1 `yin.repl` is\n   147\t  \"untouched, keep[s] running, and keep[s] their consumers ... until each\n   148\t  consumer migrates under its own plan\").\n   149\t- v1 `yin.repl`'s deletion is owed to \"the v1 deletion, per `dao.stream.md`\"\n   150\t  (`dao.jing.remote.implementation-plan.md:1037`). `dao.stream.md:803-812`\n   151\t  lists what that deletion covers — the v1 transports and `dao.stream.rpc.*` —\n   152\t  and names no date and no document. **No plan currently schedules v1\n   153\t  `yin.repl`'s deletion.**\n   154\t- v1 `yin.repl` still has live consumers with no v2 counterpart:\n   155\t  `src/cljd/yin/repl/flutter.cljd:7` (the Flutter REPL-server widget, used by\n   156\t  `src/cljd/datomworld/demo/dao_gui.cljd:7` and `solar_system.cljd:10`),\n   157\t  `src/clj/yin/vm/telemetry_server/jvm.clj:5`,\n   158\t  `src/cljs/yin/vm/telemetry_server/node.cljs:4`, `src/clj/yin/repl/runner.clj`,\n   159\t  `bin/yin_repl_main.dart`, the `:yin-repl` shadow build (`shadow-cljs.edn:31`)\n   160\t  and three `deps.edn` aliases (`:68`, `:74`, `:101`). `src/cljd/yin/repl/`\n   161\t  holds only `host.cljd`; there is no v2 Flutter widget.\n   162\t\n   163\tDeleting v1 `yin.repl` here would drag the Flutter GUI demos and both\n   164\ttelemetry servers into a VM-deletion plan. Migrating it is five edits in\n   165\t`repl.cljc`, one in `flutter.cljd`, and six lines of test. So: migrate. The\n   166\tcommand surface becomes `(vm :ast-walker)`, the same shape\n   167\t`yin.repl.core:50-53` already has, and the default changes from\n   168\t`:semantic` to `:ast-walker` — the same change the divergence register\n   169\trecords as v2's user-visible change 1.\n   170\t\n   171\t**The explicit-argument defect and what catches it.** The r2 review found\n   172\tthat `flutter.cljd:60` passes `:vm-type :semantic` explicitly, so changing the\n   173\tdefault alone would leave both Flutter demos throwing at startup, and\n   174\tcompilation would not notice because `:semantic` is a keyword, not a symbol.\n   175\tThe telemetry servers (`jvm.clj:11`, `node.cljs:10`) pass only\n   176\t`:telemetry-stream` and take the default, so they are safe; `flutter.cljd` is\n   177\tthe only explicit site in the tree. Three things catch this class of defect,\n   178\tand this plan uses all three:\n   179\t\n   180\t1. **The Phase 0 keyword sweep** — a grep for the model keywords as literals,\n   181\t   not as namespaces, over every host's source (`.clj`, `.cljc`, `.cljs`,\n   182\t   `.cljd`). It is how this round found `flutter.cljd:60`; it would have found\n   183\t   it in r1 had r1 run it.\n   184\t2. **A cljc test on every host** — add to `test/yin/repl_test.cljc` a\n   185\t   `create-state-accepts-every-advertised-vm-type-test` that iterates the keys\n   186\t   of `vm-constructors` and calls `create-state` with each, and asserts that\n   187\t   `(create-state {:vm-type :semantic})` throws with `:supported [:ast-walker]`.\n   188\t   It pins the contract the Flutter widget depends on; it cannot see the\n   189\t   widget's own argument, which is why item 1 exists.\n   190\t3. **A startup smoke on a Dart host** — `flutter.cljd` cannot be required by\n   191\t   a test outside a Flutter runtime. Phase 1's criteria include compiling and\n   192\t   launching `datomworld.demo.dao-gui` as `src/cljd/datomworld/demo/dao_gui.md:41`\n   193\t   describes and confirming the server-status notifier reaches \"listening\"\n   194\t   (`repl/connection-status-text`); `start-server!` is on the launch path at\n   195\t   `dao_gui.cljd:321`. This is the only check that exercises the actual line.\n   196\t\n   197\tOne consequence to state plainly: after this, `defmacro` and every macro call\n   198\tstop working in the v1 REPL too, because v1's `ast-walker` has no\n   199\t`macro-expand` branch (divergence register, change 2). Only `semantic` ever\n   200\tevaluated macros. That is the intended outcome of the v2 scope decision, now\n   201\tapplied to v1.\n   202\t\n   203\t### D2 — `continuation-handoff` and `yin.demo` are this plan's, not \"the demo surfaces'\" [J]\n   204\t\n   205\t`dao.jing.remote.implementation-plan.md:1043-1044` and `dao.stream.md:806`\n   206\tleave \"the demo surfaces\" to their own plans. Both are read as: the surfaces\n   207\tmigrate — get a v2 twin — under their own plan. For these two files the twin\n   208\texists and is wired in (`continuation_handoff_v2.cljc`, `demo_v2.clj`), so\n   209\tthe migration is done and only the v1 file is left. A file with no consumer\n   210\tthat requires a file this plan deletes has exactly one plan that can delete\n   211\tit: this one. `dao.runtime.implementation-plan.md:219-223` names both as\n   212\tv1-VM consumers gating R4, which this plan therefore clears.\n   213\t\n   214\t### D3 — the three cljs browser demos are deleted here; the pipeline twin gets its frontends back first [J]\n   215\t\n   216\tSame reasoning as D2, with one difference: they *are* live surfaces, reachable\n   217\tfrom the `:demo` browser build (`shadow-cljs.edn:9-16`) through\n   218\t`datomworld.demo`'s picker. Their `-v2` twins sit beside them in the same\n   219\tpicker (`demo.cljs:46-58`, `:230-236`). Leaving the v1 three in place is not\n   220\tan option — the `:demo` build fails to compile without `yin.vm.register` — and\n   221\tno other document plans their removal.\n   222\t\n   223\t**A known feature gap, not a hypothetical [R].** r1 assumed the twins were\n   224\tfeature-complete and left it to Phase 0. The r2 review found, and this round\n   225\tconfirmed, that v1 `compilation_pipeline.cljs` offers Clojure, Python and PHP\n   226\tinput (CodeMirror modes at `:2-3`, compilers `yang.python`/`yang.php` at\n   227\t`:19-20`, dispatch at `:862-863`, eight Python/PHP examples at `:894-917`,\n   228\tthe selector at `:1552-1553`), while `compilation_pipeline_v2.cljs` compiles\n   229\tClojure only (`:15`, `:40`). Deleting v1 as r1 wrote it would silently remove\n   230\tPython and PHP from the public demo that `yin.chp` links to as \"Try the Live\n   231\tDemo\". That is a product regression, and nobody has signed off on one.\n   232\t\n   233\t**Disposition [J]:** the plan does not regress. Before v1 is deleted, port the\n   234\tlanguage selector, the two compile branches, and the Python/PHP example\n   235\tsnippets into `compilation_pipeline_v2.cljs`. The cost is small and the\n   236\tpieces are all in place: `yang.python` and `yang.php` are `.cljc`\n   237\t(`src/cljc/yang/`) and produce the same `:yin/*` AST `yang.clojure` does, so\n   238\tthe twin's Source→AST step gains a `case` on language and nothing downstream\n   239\tchanges; the CodeMirror language packages are already dependencies. What is\n   240\t*not* ported is the rest of v1's 1856-line UI; the twin keeps its own shape.\n   241\tIf the owner would rather drop Python and PHP from the demo, that is their\n   242\texplicit decision to record in this section, with the `yin.chp` copy checked\n   243\tfor claims it would break — the plan's default is the port, so no sign-off is\n   244\tneeded to proceed as written.\n   245\t\n   246\tThe other two pairs (`equation_plotter`, `continuation_stream`) still get the\n   247\tPhase 0 diff. Neither mentions Python or PHP, and their line counts are within\n   248\ta few percent of their twins', but \"similar size\" is not \"same features\", so\n   249\tthe check stands.\n   250\t\n   251\t### D4 — `bytecode_bench` is deleted, not trimmed [J]\n   252\t\n   253\tRecorded in the census table. The alternative — keep an `--ast-walker-only`\n   254\tbench named \"bytecode\" with no bytecode model in it — is the kind of leftover\n   255\tthe repo's minimal-diff preference argues against, and the dao.runtime plan\n   256\talready lists the bench as a v1 consumer to clear. The five aliases go with\n   257\tit; `docs/cesk-space-optimization.md` (`:20`, `:158-173`, `:206`, `:218`) and\n   258\t`docs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md:401` reference `clj -M:bench`\n   259\tand the profile aliases and are covered by Phase 2's status notes.\n   260\t\n   261\t### D5 — the v1 demo hashes stay as aliases to the v2 entries [J]\n   262\t\n   263\t**[R]** `public/chp/yin.chp:18` advertises `/demo.html#pipeline` as \"Try the\n   264\tLive Demo\". r1 removed the `#pipeline` route, which would have turned a\n   265\tpublic link into the picker's home page. No other document under `public/`,\n   266\t`docs/`, `README.md` or `src/` links to a v1 demo hash.\n   267\t\n   268\t**Disposition [J]:** keep the three v1 hashes in `hash->demo` and point them\n   269\tat the v2 ids (`\"#pipeline\"` → `:pipeline-v2`, and likewise for `#plotter` and\n   270\t`#continuation`). `demo->hash` drops the v1 rows, so the address bar shows the\n   271\tv2 hash once the user is there. `yin.chp` is not edited: an external link that\n   272\tkeeps working is better than an edited link, and any bookmark or third-party\n   273\tlink to `#pipeline` keeps working too. Phase 1's criteria include opening\n   274\t`/demo.html#pipeline` and landing on the v2 pipeline.\n   275\t\n   276\t### D6 — one deletion set, one change\n   277\t\n   278\tPer the dependency analysis above. A single commit deletes the five `src`\n   279\tfiles, the ten test files, the nine consumer files, and applies the eight\n   280\tmigrations; the build is green after it. Splitting into \"VMs then macro\"\n   281\twould require the two macro tests to move to the first commit anyway,\n   282\tleaving the second commit as one orphaned file, which is not worth a phase.\n   283\tThe r2 review confirmed an atomic commit exposes no partially-edited state.\n   284\t\n   285\t## Phases\n   286\t\n   287\t### Phase 0 — pre-checks, no edits\n   288\t\n   289\t1. Run the three sweeps and confirm the census is still exact. Every hit must\n   290\t   be a row in the census or a documented non-hit (e.g. `dao.gui.compiler`'s\n   291\t   layout keyword `:stack`, which is unrelated). A hit that is not is a new\n   292\t   consumer and gets a row before anything is deleted.\n   293\t   ```\n   294\t   # namespaces, every host and config\n   295\t   grep -rnE \"yin\\.vm\\.(space|semantic|stack|register|macro|wasm)\\b\" \\\n   296\t     src test bin deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn public\n   297\t   # model keywords as literals (catches explicit :vm-type arguments)\n   298\t   grep -rnE \":(semantic|register|stack|space)\\b\" \\\n   299\t     --include='*.clj' --include='*.cljc' --include='*.cljs' --include='*.cljd' src test\n   300\t   # launchers and aliases for deleted entry points\n   301\t   grep -rnE \"bytecode-bench|register-bench-cljd\\b|register_bench_cljd\\b|yin\\.demo\\b\" \\\n   302\t     deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn bin\n   303\t   ```\n   304\t2. Diff `equation_plotter.cljs` and `continuation_stream.cljs` against their\n   305\t   `-v2` twins for user-visible features (D3). Record the result in the\n   306\t   commit message. Any gap is closed in the twin first. The pipeline gap is\n   307\t   already known and is a Phase 1 work item, not a check.\n   308\t3. Confirm `test/yang/clojure_test.clj` is the right home for\n   309\t   `test-nested-defn-ast-walker` (it tests `yang.clojure/compile-program`).\n   310\t\n   311\t### Phase 1 — the deletion set\n   312\t\n   313\tPort first (so the browser demo never loses a feature between commits, even\n   314\tthough this lands as one commit): the Python/PHP frontends into\n   315\t`compilation_pipeline_v2.cljs` (D3).\n   316\t\n   317\tDelete:\n   318\t\n   319\t- `src/cljc/yin/vm/{semantic, register, stack, space, macro}.cljc`\n   320\t- `src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff.cljc`\n   321\t- `src/clj/yin/demo.clj`\n   322\t- `src/cljs/datomworld/demo/{compilation_pipeline, continuation_stream, equation_plotter}.cljs`\n   323\t- `src/cljd/yin/register_bench_cljd.cljd` and `bin/register_bench_cljd.dart`\n   324\t- `src/clj/yin/vm/bytecode_bench.clj` and its five `deps.edn` aliases\n   325\t  (`:bench`, `:profile`, `:profile-fast`, `:profile-cesk-space`,\n   326\t  `:profile-ast-walker`; `deps.edn:17-30`)\n   327\t- `test/yin/vm/{semantic, register, stack, space, macro, parity, stream_listen}_test.cljc`\n   328\t- `test/yang/macro_test.clj` (after moving its walker test)\n   329\t- `test/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff_test.cljc`\n   330\t- `test/datomworld/demo/vm_state_keys_test.cljs`\n   331\t- `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/wasm-vm.md`\n   332\t\n   333\tMigrate, exactly as the census table specifies: `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc`,\n   334\t`src/cljd/yin/repl/flutter.cljd`, `src/cljs/datomworld/demo.cljs`,\n   335\t`test/yin/vm/test_utils.cljc`, `test/yin/vm/runtime_regression_test.cljc`,\n   336\t`test/yin/vm/telemetry_test.cljc`, `test/yin/repl_test.cljc` (five edits plus\n   337\tthe new deftest from D1), `test/yang/clojure_test.clj` (receives one deftest).\n   338\t\n   339\tAlso in this change, because they describe the code being changed:\n   340\t\n   341\t- `src/cljc/yin/repl/core.cljc:50-52` docstring and\n   342\t  `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:55-58` say the remaining evaluators\n   343\t  \"follow in the VM plan\". They do not; rewrite to say they were deleted under\n   344\t  this plan and `:ast-walker` is the only evaluator.\n   345\t- `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:81` (v1 REPL command table) and\n   346\t  `docs/design/yin-repl-design.md` (`:10`, `:60`, `:76`, `:121`, `:150-155`,\n   347\t  `:208`, `:249`, `:357-358`): the backend list and the `:semantic` default.\n   348\t\n   349\t**Criteria:**\n   350\t\n   351\t- `clj -M:test`, the shadow `:test` node build, and `clojure -M:cljd test`\n   352\t  all pass; the `:demo` browser build compiles.\n   353\t- `clj -M:clj-yin-repl` starts; `(vm :ast-walker)` and `(reset)` work;\n   354\t  `(vm :register)` reports the error naming `[:ast-walker]` as supported.\n   355\t- `clj -M -m yin.demo-v2` still prints 5050.\n   356\t- `datomworld.demo.dao-gui` compiles per `dao_gui.md:41` and, launched on a\n   357\t  Dart host, its REPL server reaches \"listening\" (D1 item 3).\n   358\t- `/demo.html#pipeline` opens the v2 pipeline (D5); in it, a Python and a PHP\n   359\t  example compile and run (D3).\n   360\t- All three Phase 0 sweeps return only hits under `docs/` and `collab/`, plus\n   361\t  the documented non-hits.\n   362\t\n   363\t### Phase 2 — prose that names what was deleted\n   364\t\n   365\tHistorical documents get a one-line status note at the top, not a rewrite:\n   366\t\n   367\t- `docs/cesk-space-optimization.md` (already \"superseded\"; add that\n   368\t  `yin.vm.space` and the `:bench`/`:profile-*` aliases it cites are deleted)\n   369\t- `docs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md:163,401` (names\n   370\t  `yin.vm.space` as \"closest to this shape\" and cites `clj -M:bench`)\n   371\t- `docs/cross-language-macro.md:46` (the design depends on\n   372\t  `yin.vm.macro/expand-all`, which no longer exists)\n   373\t- `docs/design/yin.vm-portability.md:217`\n   374\t- `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin-defmacro.md` and `bytecode-vm-optimization.md`\n   375\t- `docs/agy-test.md:59,104` (proposes fuzzing a deleted wasm backend)\n   376\t\n   377\tLiving documents get their facts corrected:\n   378\t\n   379\t- `docs/design/yin.vm.divergence-register.md:30` says \"`yin.vm.macro` was\n   380\t  required only by `semantic`\". It was required by all four models. Correct\n   381\t  the sentence; the conclusion (the walker has no macro branch) stands.\n   382\t- `docs/design/dao.runtime.implementation-plan.md:219-223`: strike the\n   383\t  consumers this plan cleared — `yin.demo`, `yin.vm.bytecode-bench`,\n   384\t  `yin.register-bench-cljd`, `datomworld.demo.continuation-handoff`,\n   385\t  `datomworld.demo.continuation-stream`, `datomworld.demo.compilation-pipeline`,\n   386\t  `datomworld.demo.equation-plotter`, and `datomworld.demo` itself (after this\n   387\t  plan it requires no `yin.vm.*` namespace; its remaining v1 dependence is\n   388\t  `dao.stream` through `yin_repl.cljs` and `telemetry_viewer.cljs`, which is\n   389\t  the stream gate, not the VM gate). Leave `yin.repl` v1 and `dao.await`.\n   390\t- `docs/design/dao.stream.md:806-808` is accurate as written and is left alone.\n   391\t\n   392\t**Criteria:** no file outside `collab/` and `docs/orchestrator-log.md` refers\n   393\tto a deleted namespace, model, alias or launcher as if it existed. Verified by\n   394\tthe three Phase 0 sweeps plus\n   395\t`grep -rn \"SemanticVM\\|RegisterVM\\|StackVM\" docs src`.\n   396\t\n   397\t## Completion criteria\n   398\t\n   399\tEvery file this plan touches, in one list, so the reviewer can tick it:\n   400\t\n   401\t- Deleted (26): the 5 models/engine, `continuation_handoff.cljc`, `demo.clj`,\n   402\t  3 cljs demos, `register_bench_cljd.cljd`, `bin/register_bench_cljd.dart`,\n   403\t  `bytecode_bench.clj`, 7 VM tests, `yang/macro_test.clj`,\n   404\t  `continuation_handoff_test.cljc`, `vm_state_keys_test.cljs`, `wasm-vm.md`.\n   405\t- Migrated (9): `repl.cljc`, `flutter.cljd`, `demo.cljs`,\n   406\t  `compilation_pipeline_v2.cljs`, `test_utils.cljc`,\n   407\t  `runtime_regression_test.cljc`, `telemetry_test.cljc`, `repl_test.cljc`,\n   408\t  `yang/clojure_test.clj`.\n   409\t- Config (1): `deps.edn` loses the five aliases `:bench`, `:profile`,\n   410\t  `:profile-fast`, `:profile-cesk-space`, `:profile-ast-walker`.\n   411\t- Prose (13): the two `yin.repl` sources, `yin.repl.md`,\n   412\t  `yin-repl-design.md`, the six historical docs, the divergence register,\n   413\t  the dao.runtime plan.\n   414\t- Unchanged but verified (1): `public/chp/yin.chp:18` still resolves.\n   415\t- Build green on clj, cljs (`:test` and `:demo`), cljd; the Dart-host smoke\n   416\t  and the browser-demo checks under Phase 1 pass.\n   417\t\n   418\t## Boundary — what stays, and what is owed elsewhere\n   419\t\n   420\t**Stays after this plan, deliberately:** the v1 ast-walker lineage —\n   421\t`yin.vm`, `yin.vm.{ast-walker, engine, ffi, telemetry, stream-driver,\n   422\truntime-adapter}`, `dao.runtime`, and their tests. They are still required by\n   423\tv1 `yin.repl` (`repl.cljc:17-18`), `dao.await` (`await.cljc:25-27`) and\n   424\t`test/yin/vm/parity_test.cljc:16` (v2 parity is asserted against v1 in the\n   425\tsame process). Deleting them is the second slice of the v1 VM deletion that\n   426\t`dao.stream.md:806` assigns to this document's name; it needs v1 `yin.repl`'s\n   427\tconsumers (D1) and `dao.await`'s migration to `dao.await` resolved first,\n   428\tand no document schedules either.\n   429\t\n   430\tThere are two different gates downstream of this plan, and r1 ran them\n   431\ttogether **[R]**. They are separated here.\n   432\t\n   433\t**Gate 1 — `dao.runtime` R4, the VM gate.** R4 is \"gated on v1\n   434\t`yin.vm.engine` no longer requiring `dao.runtime`, which is gated on the v1\n   435\tVM's ten consumers migrating\" (`dao.runtime.implementation-plan.md:352-354`,\n   436\tcensus at `:219-223`). Of those ten, this plan clears eight (the seven struck\n   437\tin Phase 2 plus `datomworld.demo`) and leaves two: v1 `yin.repl` and\n   438\t`dao.await`. Plus one the runtime plan does not list because it is a test:\n   439\t`yin.vm.parity-test`'s require of v1 `ast-walker`. **This plan does not\n   440\tclaim to open R4.** The first draft said it \"fulfills the prerequisites for\n   441\tsafely executing Phase R4\"; it clears most of the gate and names what is left.\n   442\t\n   443\t**Gate 2 — the `dao.stream` rename, the stream gate.** `dao.stream.md:790-796`\n   444\trenames `dao.stream` to `dao.stream` only \"when the last consumer has\n   445\tmigrated under its own plan and legacy `dao.stream` is deleted\". That\n   446\tconsumer list (`dao.stream.md:803-812`) is `yin.io`'s file transports with\n   447\t`dao.gui.event` and `dao.postgraphics.terminal`, `dao.runtime` (gate 1),\n   448\t`agent.tools`, the demo and server surfaces, the v1 VM lineage, and the v1\n   449\ttransports themselves. This plan removes exactly four entries from it — the\n   450\tfour models, which required v1 `dao.stream` — and touches nothing else on it.\n   451\t`datomworld.demo`, v1 `yin.repl`, both telemetry servers and the Flutter\n   452\twidget all still require v1 `dao.stream` after this plan. The stream gate is\n   453\tmuch larger than the VM gate and is not nearly done; nothing here should be\n   454\tread as implying otherwise.\n   455\t\n   456\t| owed | by | recorded where |\n   457\t|---|---|---|\n   458\t| deletion of v1 `yin.repl` with `yin.repl.flutter`, both telemetry servers, `yin.repl.runner`, `bin/yin_repl_main.dart`, the `:yin-repl` build and its aliases | the v1 deletion, once `dao_gui.cljd`/`solar_system.cljd` have a v2 REPL widget or drop the REPL | `dao.stream.md` *remaining v1 consumers*; nothing more specific exists |\n   459\t| `dao.await` off v1 `yin.vm` | `dao.await`'s own plan (`dao.runtime.implementation-plan.md:393-394`) | there |\n   460\t| v2 parity test off v1 `ast-walker` | the second VM deletion slice — parity against a deleted v1 needs pinned values instead | this table |\n   461\t| the second VM deletion slice (v1 walker lineage, then `dao.runtime` R4) | a successor to this plan, written when the three rows above are clear | this table; this is gate 1 |\n   462\t| the `dao.stream` rename | whoever lands the last row of `dao.stream.md:803-812`; not a VM plan | `dao.stream.md:790-796`; this is gate 2 |\n   463\t| `equation_plotter`/`continuation_stream` v1→v2 feature diffs | this plan, Phase 0 | above |\n   464\t| a v2 walker benchmark | nobody; optional | this table |\n   465\t\n   466\t## Revision history\n   467\t\n   468\t- **2026-09-10, architect r2**, against an adversarial review (gpt-6-astra) of\n   469\t  r1. Six findings, all re-verified against the tree and resolved:\n   470\t  `runtime_regression_test.cljc` moved from \"unchanged\" to \"migrated\" (it\n   471\t  requires the three models at `:8-10`; body untouched). `flutter.cljd:60`'s\n   472\t  explicit `:vm-type :semantic` added to the migration table, with the three\n   473\t  checks that catch the class (keyword sweep, cross-host `create-state` test,\n   474\t  Dart-host startup smoke). Alias count corrected to five and named;\n   475\t  `bin/register_bench_cljd.dart` given a deletion row; the Phase 0 sweep\n   476\t  widened to three greps over `src test bin deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn\n   477\t  public`. D3's \"assumption\" replaced by the verified Python/PHP frontend gap\n   478\t  in `compilation_pipeline_v2.cljs`, with a port-before-delete disposition.\n   479\t  D5 added: `#pipeline`, `#plotter`, `#continuation` kept as alias routes so\n   480\t  `yin.chp:18` keeps working. Boundary split into the R4 VM gate (this plan\n   481\t  clears eight of ten consumers) and the `dao.stream` rename gate (this\n   482\t  plan clears four entries of a much longer list). Census: 28 → 31 files.\n   483\t- **2026-09-10, architect r1.** Consumer census added (28 files; the draft\n   484\t  named 2). `wasm` dropped from the delete list — gone in `b8a6fce`. Phases 1\n   485\t  and 2 merged because both macro tests require the models. v1 `yin.repl` given\n   486\t  a migrate disposition with evidence that no plan schedules its deletion (D1).\n   487\t  `continuation-handoff`, `yin.demo`, the three cljs demos, the cljd bench and\n   488\t  `bytecode_bench` given deletion dispositions (D2–D4). End condition corrected:\n   489\t  this plan clears part of the R4 gate, not all of it. Divergence register\n   490\t  line 30 flagged as factually wrong about `macro`'s dependents.\n   491\t- **Original draft.** Three phases; two files named in completion criteria.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
