mpile the CLJD sources\n    37\t\n    38\tThe Flutter app runs generated Dart from `lib/cljd-out`, so compile CLJD before starting the app:\n    39\t\n    40\t```bash\n    41\tmise exec -- clj -M:cljd compile dao.stream.ws yin.repl datomworld.demo.dao-gui datomworld.main\n    42\t```\n    43\t\n    44\t## 2. Clean and run the app\n    45\t\n    46\t```bash\n    47\tmise exec -- flutter clean\n    48\tmise exec -- flutter run\n    49\t```\n    50\t\n    51\tThe app should show the REPL demo screen with `status: listening`.\n    52\t\n    53\t### Running Flutter in China\n    54\t\n    55\tIf `flutter run` stalls during Android build with output like:\n    56\t\n    57\t```text\n    58\tRunning Gradle task 'assembleDebug'...\n    59\t[        ] Downloading https://storage.googleapis.com/download.flutter.io/...\n    60\t```\n    61\t\n    62\tthe blocker is usually not your app code. The Android build is trying to fetch Flutter engine artifacts from Google storage.\n    63\t\n    64\t`mise.toml` can point `mise` at the China mirror for the initial Flutter SDK download, but Android Gradle still needs the mirror environment variables in the process that runs `flutter`.\n    65\t\n   310\t                               (fn [] (.pop (m/Navigator.of ctx)))\n   311\t                               .child\n   312\t                               (m/Text \"Close\"))])))\n   313\t          nil)\n   314\t        .child\n   315\t        (m/Text \"Remote REPL Info\")))))\n   316\t\n   317\t\n   318\t(defn start!\n   319\t  []\n   320\t  (show-sample-frame!)\n   321\t  (flutter-repl/start-server! {:extra-primitives (extra-primitives)}))\n   322\t\n   323\t\n   324\t(defn stop!\n   325\t  []\n   326\t  (flutter-repl/stop-server!))\n   327\t\n   328\t\n   329\t(defn view\n   330\t  []\n   331\t  (m/Scaffold\n   332\t    .appBar\n   333\t    (m/AppBar .title (m/Text \"dao.gui demo\"))\n   334\t    .body\n   335\t    (m/LayoutBuilder\n   336\t      .builder\n   337\t      (fn [_ ^m/BoxConstraints constraints]\n   338\t        (let [max-width (.-maxWidth constraints)\n   339\t              content-width (if (< max-width 720.0) max-width 720.0)]\n   340\t          (m/Center\n   341\t            .child\n   342\t            (m/SizedBox\n   343\t              .width\n   344\t              content-width\n   345\t              .child\n   346\t              (m/ListView\n   347\t                .padding\n   348\t                (m/EdgeInsets.all 16.0)\n   349\t                .children\n   350\t                [(repl-info-button) (m/SizedBox .height 16.0)\n   351\t                 (m/Text \"Remote Frame Surface\"\n   352\t                         .style\n   353\t                         (m/TextStyle .fontWeight m/FontWeight.bold))\n   354\t                 (m/SizedBox .height 8.0)\n   355\t                 (m/LayoutBuilder\n   356\t                   .builder\n   357\t                   (fn [_ ^m/BoxConstraints constraints]\n   358\t                     (let [max-width (.-maxWidth constraints)\n   359\t                           surface-width (max 0.0 (- max-width 24.0))\n   360\t                           surface-height (* surface-width\n    44\t(defn stop-server!\n    45\t  \"Stops the active REPL server and clears the server status.\"\n    46\t  []\n    47\t  (when-let [server @repl-server]\n    48\t    (when-let [stop! (:stop! server)] (stop!))\n    49\t    (reset! repl-server nil)\n    50\t    (set! (.-value ^m/ValueNotifier server-status) \"stopped\")\n    51\t    :stopped))\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t(defn start-server!\n    55\t  \"Starts the REPL server on the specified port (default: 7778 on iOS, 7777 elsewhere) and populates the device-ip and server-status notifiers.\"\n    56\t  [{:keys [port extra-primitives], :or {port default-port}}]\n    57\t  (stop-server!)\n    58\t  (reset! active-clients 0)\n    59\t  (reset! repl-state\n    60\t          (-> (repl/create-state {:vm-type :semantic})\n    61\t              (update :vm update :primitives merge (or extra-primitives {}))))\n    62\t  (reset! repl-server\n    63\t          (repl/serve!\n    64\t            repl-state\n    65\t            port\n    66\t            {;; Unlike the CLI entrypoints, this server is meant to be reached\n    67\t             ;; from another device on the same LAN (see device-ip/\n    68\t             ;; interface-addresses above), so it opts back into binding all\n    69\t             ;; interfaces rather than yin.repl/serve!'s localhost-only default.\n    70\t             :host \"0.0.0.0\",\n    71\t             :on-connect (fn [_stream]\n    72\t                           (let [client-count (swap! active-clients inc)]\n    73\t                             (set! (.-value ^m/ValueNotifier server-status)\n    74\t                                   (repl/connection-status-text client-count)))),\n    75\t             :on-disconnect (fn [_stream]\n    76\t                              (let [client-count (swap! active-clients\n    77\t                                                        (fn [n] (max 0 (dec n))))]\n    78\t                                (set! (.-value ^m/ValueNotifier server-status)\n    79\t                                      (repl/connection-status-text client-count))))}))\n    80\t  (set! (.-value ^m/ValueNotifier server-status)\n    81\t        (repl/connection-status-text @active-clients))\n    82\t  (load-device-ip!))\n    83\t\n    84\t\n(ns yin.repl-test\n  (:require #?(:cljs [cljs.test :refer-macros [async]])\n            #?(:clj [clojure.edn :as edn]\n               :cljs [cljs.reader :as edn]\n               :cljd [clojure.edn :as edn])\n            [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream :as ds]\n            [dao.stream.apply :as dao-apply]\n            [dao.stream.ws]\n            [dao.stream.rpc.client :as rpc-client]\n            [dao.stream.rpc.ws :as rpc-ws]\n            [yin.repl :as repl]))\n\n\n(defn- fact?\n  [datoms attr value]\n  (boolean (some #(and (= attr (nth % 1)) (= value (nth % 2))) datoms)))\n\n\n#?(:cljs (defmacro async-deftest\n           [name & body]\n           `(deftest ~name\n              (async ~'done\n                     (-> (identity nil)\n                         ~@(map (fn [form] `(.then (fn [] ~form))) body)\n                         (.then (fn [] (~'done)))\n                         (.catch (fn [e#] (is nil e#) (~'done))))))))\n\n\n(deftest eval-input-dispatch-test\n  #?(:clj\n     (do\n       (testing \"Clojure source evaluation persists VM state across inputs\"\n         (let [[state-1 result-1] @(repl/eval-input (repl/create-state)\n                                                    \"(+ 20 22)\")\n               [state-2 result-2] @(repl/eval-input state-1 \"(def x 10)\")\n               [_state-3 result-3] @(repl/eval-input state-2 \"x\")]\n           (is (= \"42\" result-1))\n           (is (= \"10\" result-2))\n           (is (= \"10\" result-3))))\n       (testing \"AST maps are evaluated directly\"\n         (let [[_state result] @(repl/eval-input (repl/create-state)\n                                                 \"{:type :literal :value 7}\")]\n           (is (= \"7\" result))))\n33:(def ^:private vm-constructors\n164:   (when-not (contains? vm-constructors vm-type)\n167:                      :supported (vec (keys vm-constructors))})))\n168:   (let [constructor (get vm-constructors vm-type)\n333:  ;; ' (quote), # (dispatch), etc. are supported in REPL input.\n490:    (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported Yin REPL language\" {:lang lang}))))\n517:    (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported Yin REPL language\" {:lang (:lang state)}))))\n557:           (when-not (contains? vm-constructors vm-type)\n560:                              :supported (vec (keys vm-constructors))})))\n   790\t## The v2 namespace is transient\n   791\t\n   792\t`dao.stream` exists to protect a working system while its consumers move,\n   793\tnot to live forever. When the last consumer has migrated under its own plan\n   794\tand legacy `dao.stream` is deleted, **`dao.stream` is renamed to\n   795\t`dao.stream`** — decided, not left open. An undecided coexistence of both\n   796\tnamespaces is a defect of the migration, not a steady state.\n   797\t\n   798\tThis is recorded here because the plan that carried it,\n   799\t`dao.stream.implementation-plan.md`, was consumed when its phases\n   800\tcompleted; the decision it left open outlived it, and a transient plan is\n   801\tsafe to delete only once nothing in it is still owed.\n   802\t\n   803\tThe remaining v1 consumers, each migrating under its own plan:\n   804\t`yin.io`'s file transports with `dao.gui.event` and\n   805\t`dao.postgraphics.terminal`, `dao.runtime` (gated on the v1 VM's deletion),\n   806\t`agent.tools`, and the demo and server surfaces. The v1 VM lineage is deleted\n   807\trather than migrated, under `yin.vm-consumers.implementation-plan.md`,\n   808\tbecause a v2 twin already exists for every one of its consumers. So are the v1\n   809\ttransports themselves — `dao.stream.{apply, file, file-input-stream,\n   810\tfile-output-stream, http, link, ringbuffer, udp, ws}` and `dao.stream.rpc.*`,\n   811\twith their ClojureDart siblings: they are v1's own implementation, not\n   812\tconsumers of it, and they go when it does rather than acquiring v2 twins one\n   813\tby one.\n   814\t\n   815\t`dao.space` is done: `query`, `index` and `transactor` require `dao.stream`,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
